# v0.24.0 — Hub node development special

## Scenarios are CLI-first plays of the live software (2026-08-21)

`docs/scenarios/` is now the operator manual for the software **as it runs**, not a mix of curl tickets and planned features. `aitbc` is the primary tool in every play. Curl / `journalctl` / `pytest` are validation only.

- Added `docs/DESIGN_CYCLE.md`: current closed economic loop, maturity map, gaps, and P0-P2 wish list.
- Intermediate scenarios 21-36 rewritten onto real CLI groups (`start`, `system`, `bridge`, `ai`, `gpu`, `market`, `transactions`, `exchange-island`, `pool-hub`, …).
- Beginner 06 uses `AIT/ETH` only (`exchange-island` does not accept `AIT/BTC`). Beginner 11 leads with `aitbc ipfs` / `aitbc oracle`. Beginner 17 distinguishes `aitbc governance` (port 8105) from `aitbc operations governance` (RPC).
- CLI gap closed: `aitbc ai submit --currency` so scenario 25 can force `payment_status=skipped` without raw HTTP.

## V23-95 — Corrected ML circuits ported to the build tree

The `modular_ml_components` and `ml_training_verification` circuits were corrected in the coordinator-api tree under V23-94; this release ports the same fixed-point learning-rate checks to the `apps/zk-circuits` build tree and re-runs the ceremony so both trees hold byte-identical, contributed keys. `tests/unit/test_v2395_zk_circuit_tree_parity.py` now fails if the two trees diverge again.

## V23-96 — Pool Hub serves /health and describes outages instead of crashing

`pool-hub` now exposes a real `/health` endpoint. Before this change the `/health` path returned 404 and the monitoring infrastructure never watched the service. The monitoring and `health_check.sh endpoints` checks now treat `aitbc-pool-hub` as a first-class service.

## V23-97 — `is_not` operator fixed so billing sync can build a query

The Pool Hub SLA/billing query builder now emits the `is_not` operator correctly, allowing `/v1/sla/violations?resolved=true` to return 200 instead of 500. The CLI also aborts with a clear message when asked for per-pool SLA or when the host is unreachable.

## CLI — raw JSON, `balance_ait`, and `aitbc update`

- `aitbc account get` now shows `balance_ait` alongside the raw compute-seconds balance.
- `aitbc wallet balance` preserves the daemon's `balance`/`balance_ait` fields.
- `aitbc --output json` returns unwrapped machine-readable JSON.
- `aitbc update` pulls the latest `main` and runs `scripts/deployment/update.sh` in one command.

## V23-92 follow-up — shop/follower nodes stop treating hub-only services as local

`aitbc-exchange` (8106) and `aitbc-agent-coordinator` (8107) are hub-only. V23-92 already stopped coin-request notifications from defaulting to `localhost:8107`. The same default was still sitting in CLI config, pool-hub miner registration, and `health_check.sh`, so a shop node would report those units as down. Off-hub URLs now come from `HUB_DISCOVERY_URL` / `HUB_AGENT_URL` / `HUB_EXCHANGE_URL` in `/etc/aitbc/{blockchain,node}.env` (no baked-in hostname). `health_check.sh` now resolves the node role the same way `setup.sh` does and probes only that role's units and HTTP ports.

## Shop-chain fork recovery and live scenario follow-ups

Replay of Scenario 34 on 2026-08-20 found the shop node (`aitbc3`) forked from the hub at height 6815 (local proposer `0x19e7e376…` vs hub genesis). Bulk sync then logged `Unhandled import case` on every next-height import because the parent was not the shop tip.

- `import_block` now reports that case as `diverged=True` (`Divergent chain: next block parent … is not our head …`) instead of falling through.
- Shop was reset with `scripts/ops/reset-follower-to-genesis.sh` (DB backups left on disk) and pull-synced back to hub height.
- `aitbc market offer` as root can load `aitbc`-owned `island_credentials.json` (mode 0600). Importing the CLI as a non-root service user no longer crashes on unreadable `/etc/aitbc/blockchain-secrets.env`.
- Scenario 34 JWT generation uses `aitbc.auth.create_access_token`; exchange examples use `/api/orders/orderbook` and `POST /api/orders` with `X-Api-Key`.

## Live verification

After the merges and restart on the hub node:
- `/health` returns 200 with `db`, `redis`, and `miners_online` status.
- `/v1/sla/violations?resolved=true` returns 200.
- `aitbc pool-hub status` and `aitbc pool-hub sla` return live data instead of simulated.
- `poolhub_miners_online` is exported on `/metrics` for Prometheus.

## Hub↔shop paid AI jobs and marketplace offers

This batch of fixes completes the live two-node flow between `hub.aitbc` (customer) and `aitbc3` (shop/miner):

- `ESCROW_RELEASE` transactions are now signed with the genesis wallet key before being submitted to `POST /rpc/transactions/marketplace`, so paid AI jobs settle on-chain.
- The blockchain RPC `/rpc/transactions` query and `get_chain_id()` now default an empty or missing `chain_id` to the node-configured `chain_id`.
- `GPU_MARKETPLACE` offer transactions with `amount=0` are accepted without a secp256k1 signature, while value-carrying transactions still require a valid signature.
- The `aitbc market offer` command now posts to the correct `/v1/marketplace/offer` endpoint (the old `/v1/marketplace/software-services` path did not exist).
- `qa-cycle.py` no longer reads `GITEA_TOKEN` from a repo file; it uses the `GITEA_TOKEN` environment variable or `~/.gitea_token`.
- Legacy `http://127.0.0.1:18000` and `18001` references were removed from test scripts, completion, and example comments.
- `scripts/testing/run_all_tests.sh` was updated to use current, valid CLI options and now passes 9/9 CLI smoke tests.

